; expect-fail: wasm — codegen uses an UNTAGGED i64 value model, so integer 0,
; boolean false, and unit all share the bit pattern 0. `if` tests truth with
; `i64.eqz`, which cannot tell 0 (truthy) from false/unit (falsy). Making 0
; truthy here needs a tagged value representation — out of scope for the
; truthiness ruling. The EIR VM and the legacy interpreter both treat 0 as
; truthy; only wasm still diverges, so this pin stays until the value model is
; tagged.
[fn main []
  [println [if 0 "zero-truthy" "zero-falsy"]]]
